    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Soak the rice noodles in hot water until they are just pliable, about 8 minutes, then drain them well. They should still be firm, because they finish cooking in the pan.",
                    "Beat the eggs, scramble them in a hot nonstick pan until just set, and slide them out onto a plate to add back at the end.",
                    "Brown the ground turkey in the same pan over high heat, breaking it into crumbles and seasoning with the salt and black pepper, until it is cooked through to 165F, then set it aside with the eggs.",
                    "Add the sliced onion, sliced red bell pepper, minced garlic, grated ginger, and chopped jalapeno, and stir-fry 4 minutes until the peppers soften but still snap.",
                    "Sprinkle the curry powder and turmeric directly into the hot pan and stir for 30 seconds until it smells toasty. Dry spice in hot oil is what makes these noodles taste like the takeout version.",
                    "Add the drained noodles and the soy sauce and toss with tongs for 3 minutes until every strand is coated gold and heated through.",
                    "Fold the turkey and egg back in, kill the heat, and stir in the green onions and most of the cilantro before moving everything into your weighed pot."
                ],
    "portion_html":  "Set the full pot on the scale, subtract the empty-pot weight you wrote down, and divide by 14. That is your per-container gram target. Lift with tongs from the bottom of the pot each time so the turkey and peppers get spread out instead of settling, then finish each with the reserved cilantro. Every bowl lands at \u003cstrong\u003e582 calories and 26 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e.",
